# Shared ESLint Configuration Package

This package provides shared ESLint configurations for different parts of the monorepo, ensuring consistent code quality and style across all apps and packages.

## Purpose

Centralize ESLint rules and configurations to maintain code consistency across:
- Next.js apps (web, desktop, docs)
- Electron main process
- React Native/Expo apps
- Node.js packages
- React libraries

## Structure

```
packages/eslint-config/
??? base.js                 # Base configuration
??? next.js                 # Next.js-specific rules
??? electron.js             # Electron-specific rules
??? react-internal.js        # React internal rules
??? react-native.js         # React Native-specific rules
??? node.js                 # Node.js-specific rules
??? package.json
??? README.md
```

## Configuration Files

### Base Configuration (`base.js`)
- Shared rules for all JavaScript/TypeScript files
- Common best practices
- Base parser and plugin setup

### Next.js Configuration (`next.js`)
- Extends base config
- Next.js-specific rules
- React Server Components support
- App Router conventions

### Electron Configuration (`electron.js`)
- Electron main process rules
- Node.js environment rules
- Security-focused rules

### React Native Configuration (`react-native.js`)
- React Native-specific rules
- Expo compatibility
- Mobile-specific patterns

### Node.js Configuration (`node.js`)
- Node.js backend/server rules
- CommonJS/ESM support

## Usage

### In Package.json
```json
{
  "eslintConfig": {
    "extends": "@repo/eslint-config/next"
  }
}
```

### In ESLint Config Files
```javascript
module.exports = {
  extends: ["@repo/eslint-config/next"],
  // ... other config
};
```

## Best Practices

### Extending Configs
- Always extend base config first
- Add platform-specific configs
- Override only when necessary
- Document any custom rules

### Rule Updates
- Update rules carefully
- Test across all consuming packages
- Maintain backward compatibility
- Document breaking changes

### Configuration
- Keep configs focused
- Avoid duplication
- Use shared plugins
- Document any special rules

## Integration

### Consuming Packages
- Apps extend appropriate config
- Packages use base or specific config
- Override locally if needed
- Keep consistent across monorepo

### Maintenance
- Update ESLint plugins regularly
- Review rule changes
- Test in all consuming apps
- Maintain compatibility

## Important Notes

- Changes affect all consuming apps
- Test rule changes carefully
- Maintain backward compatibility
- Document configuration options
- Keep configs simple and focused
